---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import LegalHeader from "../components/legal/LegalHeader.astro";
import GuideNav from "../components/help/GuideNav.astro";
import Callout from "../components/help/Callout.astro";

const sections = [
  { id: "who", label: "Who we are" },
  { id: "collect", label: "What we collect" },
  { id: "use", label: "How we use it" },
  { id: "share", label: "Who sees it" },
  { id: "providers", label: "Service providers" },
  { id: "chats", label: "Chats and reports" },
  { id: "status", label: "Online status" },
  { id: "notifications", label: "Notifications" },
  { id: "storage", label: "Keeping and deleting" },
  { id: "security", label: "Security" },
  { id: "rights", label: "Your choices and rights" },
  { id: "children", label: "Children" },
  { id: "transfers", label: "Where data is kept" },
  { id: "cookies", label: "Cookies and the web app" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact us" },
];
---

<Page
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What personal information NyasaBuy collects, why, who can see it, how long we keep it, and the choices and rights you have."
>
  <LegalHeader
    title="Privacy Policy"
    intro="What we collect, why we collect it, who sees it, and the control you have. We have tried to explain it in plain words."
    updated="22 November 2026"
  />
  <GuideNav items={sections} />

  <article class="guide">
    <section id="summary">
      <Callout title="The short version" tone="good">
        <ul>
          <li>
            We collect what we need to run a marketplace: your account, your
            listings and orders, your chats, and payment references.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong>
          </li>
          <li>
            We do not see or keep your full card number or mobile money PIN.
            Our payment partner handles those.
          </li>
          <li>
            Other users see only what is needed to trade with you, such as your
            name or shop name, photo, location and ratings. They do not see
            your email or phone number unless you share them.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can change your details, switch off your online status, and
            delete your account from the app.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Callout>
    </section>

    <section id="who">
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        NyasaBuy ("<strong>we</strong>", "<strong>us</strong>") runs a
        marketplace in Malawi through our apps and website. We decide why and
        how your personal information is used, which makes us the
        "<strong>controller</strong>" of it. This policy applies to everyone
        who uses NyasaBuy as a buyer, a seller, or a visitor, and should be
        read with our <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We handle personal information in line with the laws of Malawi that
        protect it, including its data protection and electronic transactions
        laws.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="collect">
      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <h3>Information you give us</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account details:</strong> your email address, your password
          (kept in a protected form, never readable by us), your name, a
          username, a profile photo, and your phone number and location (town
          or area) where you give them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sign-in with Google:</strong> if you choose Google, we get
          your name, email address and profile picture from Google. We never
          see your Google password.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Seller details:</strong> when you apply to sell, your business
          or shop name, what you sell, contact details, and anything else the
          application asks for to check who you are.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Payout details:</strong> the mobile money number or bank
          account you want your earnings sent to, and its operator or bank.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Listings:</strong> titles, descriptions, photos, prices,
          categories, condition, quantity and location.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Messages:</strong> the chats you have with buyers and
          sellers, including offers, quantities, agreed prices, delivery times,
          receipts and the messages you edit (we keep the earlier versions).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reviews, reports and disputes:</strong> ratings and reviews
          you write, reports you make about people, listings or orders, and
          the details and evidence you add.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Things you save:</strong> your cart, wishlist and saved
          items.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>When you contact us:</strong> what you write to us and any
          files you send.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Information created when you use NyasaBuy</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Orders and payments:</strong> what was bought, the amount, the
          status, delivery times, payment references, refunds, withdrawals and
          boosts. We do not keep full card numbers or PINs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sign-in records:</strong> when you sign in, the sign-in method,
          the approximate device and browser, and the network (IP) address. We
          use this to protect accounts and spot suspicious sign-ins.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Activity:</strong> which days you were active, and your
          online status and "last seen" time (see section 7). We use this to
          show status and to understand how many people use the platform.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Device and notification details:</strong> a token that lets us
          send notifications to your phone or browser, if you allow them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical information:</strong> app version, device type,
          error reports, and the time of requests, to keep the platform working
          and secure.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Notifications:</strong> a record of the alerts we sent you
          about your orders, messages and listings.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Information we do not ask for</h3>
      <p>
        We do not ask for your exact GPS position, your contacts list, or your
        other apps' data. Your location on NyasaBuy is the town or area you
        type in, and the location on your listings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="use">
      <h2>3. How we use it, and why</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>What we do</th><th>Why we are allowed to</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Create and run your account, show your profile and listings,
                let you chat, order and pay, and send you order updates.
              </td>
              <td>It is needed to give you the service you asked for.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Take payments, hold them, pay sellers, send refunds, and keep
                payment records.
              </td>
              <td>It is needed for the service, and we must keep financial records.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Check sellers, prevent scams and fraud, investigate reports and
                disputes, enforce our Terms, and keep accounts secure.
              </td>
              <td>
                It is our legitimate interest in keeping people safe, and
                sometimes a legal duty.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Send notifications and emails about your account, orders,
                messages and safety (including one-time codes).
              </td>
              <td>It is part of the service.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Improve the app, fix problems, and understand how many people
                use it, using summaries of activity.
              </td>
              <td>It is our legitimate interest in running a good service.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Show featured listings and recommend relevant items by
                category and location.
              </td>
              <td>It is part of the service you use.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Comply with the law, answer legal requests, and protect our
                rights.
              </td>
              <td>It is a legal duty, or our legitimate interest.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Things that need your agreement, such as turning on
                notifications on your device.
              </td>
              <td>Your consent. You can withdraw it at any time.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        We do not use your information for advertising by other companies, and
        we do not use automated decisions that have a legal effect on you
        without a person being able to review them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="share">
      <h2>4. Who can see your information</h2>
      <h3>Other users</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Everyone</strong> can see your public profile: your shop or
          display name, username, profile photo, general location, ratings and
          reviews, and your listings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The person you trade with</strong> can see your chat with
          them, and what they need to complete the order, such as your name
          and the delivery location you give. Your email address and phone
          number are not shown to other users unless you put them in a chat or
          listing yourself. Please do not share personal details you do not
          want the other person to have.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not put sensitive information, such as ID numbers, passwords or
          one-time codes, in a chat or listing.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Our team</h3>
      <p>
        Only the staff and administrators who need it to run the platform, help
        you, review reports, or stop fraud can see account and order
        information. Administrator access is protected and attempts to enter
        the admin area by people who are not administrators are recorded.
      </p>
      <h3>Others, only when needed</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Service providers</strong> who help us run NyasaBuy (section
          5), under rules that limit what they can do.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Payment partners and mobile money or card providers</strong>,
          to take and send payments.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Authorities and regulators</strong>, courts or the police,
          where the law requires it or where it is needed to prevent or
          investigate a crime or serious harm.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A buyer of the business</strong> or a successor, if NyasaBuy
          is sold or reorganised, who must keep protecting your information.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>We never sell your personal information</strong>, and we do not
        give it to advertisers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="providers">
      <h2>5. Service providers we use</h2>
      <p>
        We use trusted companies to run parts of the service. They process
        information for us, or for you, and may only use it to provide that
        service. They include:
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Provider</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>PayChangu</td>
              <td>
                Takes payments and sends withdrawals through Airtel Money, TNM
                Mpamba and cards. It receives the amount, your payment details
                that you enter on its page, and the information needed to
                complete the payment.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Supabase</td>
              <td>
                Manages sign-in (email and password, Google sign-in) and stores
                account and app data securely.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Google (Sign-In and Firebase Cloud Messaging)</td>
              <td>
                Lets you sign in with Google, and delivers notifications to
                your phone or browser.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Resend</td>
              <td>Sends emails such as your one-time confirmation code.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Render and our hosting providers</td>
              <td>Run the servers, the web app and the admin tools.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        These providers have their own privacy policies for what they do under
        their own responsibility, such as the mobile money or card provider
        that processes your payment. We may change providers; we will keep this
        list up to date.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="chats">
      <h2>6. Chats, reports and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        Your chats are stored on our servers. We do not read them as a matter
        of routine. Our team may read a chat in these cases:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>A report.</strong> When someone reports a chat or a person,
          the report, the reason and details, and the most recent messages of
          that conversation are shown to our administrators so they can decide
          what to do. This can include messages you wrote.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>An order dispute</strong>, where the chat shows what was
          agreed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Safety or a legal duty</strong>, such as a suspected scam or
          a lawful request from the authorities.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When you edit a message, we keep the earlier version so that disputes
        can be settled fairly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="status">
      <h2>7. Online status and last seen</h2>
      <p>
        When you use the app, other users may see a green dot if you are
        online, or when you were last online. This helps people know when to
        expect a reply. <strong>You can switch this off</strong> in your
        privacy settings. If you do, other people no longer see your status or
        last seen, and you will not see theirs. We still keep the days you were
        active for security and for overall usage numbers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="notifications">
      <h2>8. Notifications</h2>
      <p>
        We send notifications about your orders, messages, offers, listings,
        boosts and account. In the app these are shown in your notifications
        list. If you allow it, we also send push notifications to your phone or
        browser. To do that we store a notification token for each of your
        devices and use Google's Firebase Cloud Messaging to deliver it. You can
        turn push notifications off in your device or browser settings at any
        time, and we will stop using the token. Emails about security, such as
        one-time codes, are always sent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="storage">
      <h2>9. How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>
        We keep information only as long as we need it for the reasons in this
        policy.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your account and profile:</strong> for as long as your account
          is open.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Orders, payments, refunds, withdrawals, boosts, reviews,
          disputes and the chats connected to them:</strong> kept after you leave,
          because the other person, the payment providers, our accounting and
          the law depend on them. We keep them for the period the law and our
          accounting needs (normally several years) and then delete or
          anonymise them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sign-in and security records:</strong> for a limited time to
          protect accounts and investigate abuse.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Notification tokens:</strong> until you stop using the device,
          sign out, or delete your account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reports and evidence:</strong> as long as needed to handle the
          case and any appeal, and to spot repeat offenders.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>When you delete your account</h3>
      <p>
        You can delete your account in the app. We remove your login so you can
        no longer sign in, take your listings off the marketplace, cancel unpaid
        purchases, remove your saved items and notification tokens, and
        anonymise your profile. Your name becomes "Deleted user" and your
        contact details, username, photo and business details are cleared.
        Records we must keep for other people, payment providers and the law
        stay, without your identifying profile details. You cannot delete the
        account while a paid order is still in progress.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="security">
      <h2>10. Keeping your information safe</h2>
      <p>
        We use sensible technical and organisational measures: encrypted
        connections, protected sign-in, access to data limited to those who
        need it, protected administrator access, limits on repeated sign-in and
        code attempts, and checks on payout changes. No system is perfectly
        secure, and we cannot promise it. You help by choosing a strong
        password, not sharing codes, and keeping your device safe. If there is
        a security incident that affects your personal information, we will
        tell you and the authorities where the law requires.
      </p>
      <Callout title="We will never ask for your password or codes" tone="safety">
        <p>
          NyasaBuy staff will never ask for your password, a one-time code or
          your mobile money PIN, by chat, phone, WhatsApp or email. If someone
          does, they are not us. Report them.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </section>

    <section id="rights">
      <h2>11. Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>You can control a lot yourself in the app:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>edit your name, photo, phone number, location and shop details;</li>
        <li>choose whether your online status and last seen are shown;</li>
        <li>turn notifications on or off on your device or browser;</li>
        <li>remove listings and withdraw them from the marketplace;</li>
        <li>delete your account.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Under Malawi's data protection law you also have rights over your
        personal information. You can ask us to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>tell you what personal information we hold about you;</li>
        <li>correct information that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
        <li>delete your information, where we have no good reason to keep it;</li>
        <li>
          limit or stop us using it in some ways, or object to how we use it;
        </li>
        <li>give you a copy of the information you gave us;</li>
        <li>
          take back a consent you gave, without affecting what we did before.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To use these rights, email us at the address in section 16. We may
        need to confirm it is really you, and we will reply within a reasonable
        time. Some information we must keep (see section 9), and we will tell
        you if that stops us from doing what you ask. If you are unhappy with
        how we handled your request or your information, you have the right to
        complain to the data protection authority in Malawi. We would
        appreciate the chance to put it right first.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="children">
      <h2>12. Children</h2>
      <p>
        NyasaBuy is for people aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect
        information about children. If you think a child has made an account,
        tell us and we will close it and delete what we can.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="transfers">
      <h2>13. Where your information is kept</h2>
      <p>
        Our service providers (section 5) may store and process information on
        servers outside Malawi. When your information goes abroad, we make sure
        the provider protects it to a standard that is in line with this policy
        and the law, for example through the contracts we have with them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="cookies">
      <h2>14. Cookies and the web app</h2>
      <p>
        When you use the NyasaBuy web app, your browser stores small pieces of
        data that are needed for it to work, such as to keep you signed in, to
        remember your settings (like light or dark mode), and to receive push
        notifications. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies. This
        website (the information pages) does not use cookies to follow you
        around.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2>15. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy when the way we work changes or the law
        changes. We will post the new version here with a new date and, for
        important changes, tell you in the app or by email. Please check back
        from time to time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>16. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        For anything about your privacy or your personal information, email{" "}
        <a href="mailto:privacy@nyasabuy.com">privacy@nyasabuy.com</a>. For
        general help, use{" "}<a href="mailto:support@nyasabuy.com">support@nyasabuy.com</a>{" "}
        or the <a href="/help">Help centre</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Page>
